# Gannet Harbor: a street circuit in the whaling town on Mercy Bay.
# Units in metres: x east, z south, from the world's north-west corner.
#
# The bay is to the west. The lap runs north up Front Street along the
# quay, out along the whaling pier and back, out along the cannery pier and
# back, east up Church Hill, and then straight down the hill into the
# ropewalk: one long fall carried into 170 m of shed. The cooper's yard at
# its far end turns it back west to Front Street. No walls: a gravel run-off
# either side that a kart can run wide onto and come back from. Only the
# pier decks, over the water, have a rail. The corners are flat: the hill is
# the only place the road leaves the level.
track gannet_harbor size 512 style harbor
title GANNET HARBOR
blurb A street circuit in an empty whaling town in the autumn fog: granite setts between the houses, out and back along two plank piers over the bay, up Church Hill, and one long fall straight down it into the dark of the ropewalk.
race laps 3 rivals 5 vehicle kart
road 14.5 bank 1.2
materials verge road_gravel
verge 0 1337 - 6
land 8 0.6
hour 7
lights 25

